First the question.  I'm sure this is a FAQ (at least by now), but where can
I ftp the binaries for 3.1.2 for MS-DOS?  (I haven't seen the FAQ lately; is
it being updated?)

And now the comment.  In nethack (new & old versions), the speed is messed
up and doesn't flow smoothly.  If, say, both me & another monster are speeded
up twice as fast, then what happens is I get 2 attacks, then it gets 2, etc.
But since we're both moving at regular speed _with_respect_to_each_other_,
we should be exchanging attacks one-for-one.  And of course both players and
monsters can move at other ratios of speed.  It would be nice in some future
patch to smooth the progression of time a bit better.
